# Build context for docker/backend.Dockerfile and docker/frontend.Dockerfile. Anything listed
# here cannot enter an image even when a Dockerfile copies the directory that holds it.

# pnpm installs these inside the image. A host copy would carry the host platform's binaries.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The frontend image builds its own bundle; a stale host dist must not ship instead.
**/dist

# Real configuration values. Both processes read environment variables, never a file, so no
# environment file belongs in an image — and an image is something you distribute.
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Coding-agent files: local only, and already outside the published repository.
.claude
CLAUDE.md

.DS_Store
